    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Question\n\n[`obsidian.nvim`](https://github.com/obsidian-nvim/obsidian.nvim) provides the ability to create notes directly from a completion‑suggestion entry when using `nvim‑cmp`. How can I achieve the same functionality with `mini.completion`?\r\n\r\nThis is what it looks like with `nvim-cmp`:\r\n<img width=\"1265\" height=\"231\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ca4bc7a8-a5fd-415e-b7ce-699ab1d18810\" />\r\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.completion</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/obsidian-nvim/obsidian.nvim\"><code class=\"notranslate\">obsidian.nvim</code></a> provides the ability to create notes directly from a completion‑suggestion entry when using <code class=\"notranslate\">nvim‑cmp</code>. How can I achieve the same functionality with <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.completion</code>?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is what it looks like with <code class=\"notranslate\">nvim-cmp</code>:<br>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/192042266/514763648-ca4bc7a8-a5fd-415e-b7ce-699ab1d18810.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3OTM1NTI4NTQsIm5iZiI6MTc5MzU1MjU1NCwicGF0aCI6Ii8xOTIwNDIyNjYvNTE0NzYzNjQ4LWNhNGJjN2E4LWE1ZmQtNDE1ZS1iN2NlLTY5OWFiMWQxODgxMC5wbmc_.uNqPSawSHMMNcRumC-ivy0ikEX4r6H7w3WmMjMCwRMI\"><img width=\"1265\" height=\"231\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/192042266/514763648-ca4bc7a8-a5fd-415e-b7ce-699ab1d18810.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3OTM1NTI4NTQsIm5iZiI6MTc5MzU1MjU1NCwicGF0aCI6Ii8xOTIwNDIyNjYvNTE0NzYzNjQ4LWNhNGJjN2E4LWE1ZmQtNDE1ZS1iN2NlLTY5OWFiMWQxODgxMC5wbmc_.uNqPSawSHMMNcRumC-ivy0ikEX4r6H7w3WmMjMCwRMI\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 231px;; aspect-ratio: 1265 / 231; background-color: var(--bgColor-muted); border-radius: 6px\" class=\"js-gh-image-fallback\"></a></p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.completion\nQuestion\nobsidian.nvim provides the ability to create notes directly from a completion‑suggestion entry when using nvim‑cmp. How can I achieve the same functionality with mini.completion?\nThis is what it looks like with nvim-cmp:",
