    "closedAt": "2025-11-15T14:56:05Z",
    "comment_count": 2,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I am afraid, there is nothing (reasonably manageable) you or 'mini.completion' can do here. The plugin seems to have a dedicated [sources for `nvim-cmp` and `blink.cmp`](https://github.com/obsidian-nvim/obsidian.nvim/tree/main/lua/obsidian/completion/sources).\r\n\r\nThe easiest way to make it work with 'mini.completion' out of the box is through a regular LSP client/server route. There seems to be an in-process LSP server, but it [doesn't support relevant completion methods](https://github.com/obsidian-nvim/obsidian.nvim/blob/450fa41a1e4c2bed481697cc66186898658ab1bc/lua/obsidian/lsp/handlers.lua#L4-L9) (`textDocument/completion`, `completionItem/resolve`).\r\n\r\nThere seems to be an open PR just for that: obsidian-nvim/obsidian.nvim#474. It is still a draft, though, and might require polishing (as it, for some reason, [forces some options onto the user](https://github.com/obsidian-nvim/obsidian.nvim/pull/474/files#diff-e55c111c453f3fbc81d438d744fdbce966f0beda3f4d07b3711e3ff7f11be2be)), but it is the good way forward.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I am afraid, there is nothing (reasonably manageable) you or 'mini.completion' can do here. The plugin seems to have a dedicated <a href=\"https://github.com/obsidian-nvim/obsidian.nvim/tree/main/lua/obsidian/completion/sources\">sources for <code class=\"notranslate\">nvim-cmp</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">blink.cmp</code></a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The easiest way to make it work with 'mini.completion' out of the box is through a regular LSP client/server route. There seems to be an in-process LSP server, but it <a href=\"https://github.com/obsidian-nvim/obsidian.nvim/blob/450fa41a1e4c2bed481697cc66186898658ab1bc/lua/obsidian/lsp/handlers.lua#L4-L9\">doesn't support relevant completion methods</a> (<code class=\"notranslate\">textDocument/completion</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">completionItem/resolve</code>).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There seems to be an open PR just for that: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3539827039\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/obsidian-nvim/obsidian.nvim/issues/474\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/obsidian-nvim/obsidian.nvim/pull/474/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/obsidian-nvim/obsidian.nvim/pull/474\">obsidian-nvim/obsidian.nvim#474</a>. It is still a draft, though, and might require polishing (as it, for some reason, <a href=\"https://github.com/obsidian-nvim/obsidian.nvim/pull/474/files#diff-e55c111c453f3fbc81d438d744fdbce966f0beda3f4d07b3711e3ff7f11be2be\">forces some options onto the user</a>), but it is the good way forward.</p>",
            "bodyText": "I am afraid, there is nothing (reasonably manageable) you or 'mini.completion' can do here. The plugin seems to have a dedicated sources for nvim-cmp and blink.cmp.\nThe easiest way to make it work with 'mini.completion' out of the box is through a regular LSP client/server route. There seems to be an in-process LSP server, but it doesn't support relevant completion methods (textDocument/completion, completionItem/resolve).\nThere seems to be an open PR just for that: obsidian-nvim/obsidian.nvim#474. It is still a draft, though, and might require polishing (as it, for some reason, forces some options onto the user), but it is the good way forward.",
